<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abish Khatun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1260–1286</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abish Khatun was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salghurids">Salghurid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, placed on the throne as a child in 1263 under Mongol supervision. She was married to Mengü-Temür, a son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> Hülegü, and coins were struck in her name. After her death in the 1280s Fars passed under the direct control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abish-khatun.jpg" alt="Abish Khatun" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Abish_Khatun_citing_Ilkhan_Abaqa_as_overlord.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
